    <string name="perm_scan_title">Bluetooth access needed</string>
    <string name="perm_scan_reason">The “Nearby devices” permission lets the app receive Bluetooth signals from your headphones: that is how it learns the battery level, the model and whether the case lid is open. The same permission tells the app which headphones are connected to the phone so it can show exactly those. The app does not get your location.</string>
    <string name="perm_location_reason">On Android 10–11 the system only delivers Bluetooth signals with the location permission. The app does not determine your location: it only reads the battery, model and case state from the headphones’ signal.</string>
    <string name="perm_denied_hint">Without the permission the battery cannot be shown. If the button does nothing, enable it in the app settings.</string>
